<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<StyleSet xmlns="http://adamantium/ui"
          xmlns:x="http://adamantium/ui/xaml/extensions">

    <!-- The focus ring for the whole application - the adorner stage draws this one style around whatever the keyboard
         reached, so what is written here is every control's focus visual.

         ONE LINE, NOT TWO. Fluent draws a thick accent ring with a thin inner line just inside it, which is how UWP
         keeps a ring legible on an accent-filled button. A Mac does not layer two lines: it puts a single wide band of
         accent around the control and lets its TRANSLUCENCE do the work the second line does elsewhere - over an
         accent-filled control the band goes darker rather than disappearing, because it is the same blue at partial
         alpha over the blue beneath it.

         WIDER AND SOFTER: 3 against Fluent's 2, at 60% - a Mac's ring reads as a halo the control is sitting in, not as
         a border it has grown. The full-strength accent is reserved for things that are FILLED with it.

         The OUTSET is left exactly as the borrowed set had it, and that is not laziness: a ring that stands off its
         control is clipped by whatever clips the control, and the adorner's arrange takes the outset into its size but
         not its position, so an offset ring comes out lopsided. Both are seam bugs, both are written down, and until
         they are fixed a Mac-accurate standing-off ring would look worse here than a tracing one. -->

    <Style Selector="FocusAdorner">
        <Setter Property="Outset" Value="{ResourceReference FocusRingOutset}"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="FocusAdorner">
                    <Grid IsHitTestVisible="False">
                        <Border BorderThickness="3"
                                Opacity="0.6"
                                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefault}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding AdornedCornerRadius}"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

</StyleSet>
